schema: "0.4"
id: sem-fact-ux-design
type: image
quality: high
product_targets:
  - semtext.dev
tags:
  - semtext
  - sem-fact
  - ux-design
  - reference

prompt:
  text: |
    UX design sheet for the SemText `<sem-fact>` element — the atomic
    statement/conclusion pair inside a `sem-facts` container. The element
    has three display modes (`view-as`); show one example reading page per
    mode, stacked vertically, rendered in the minimal-tech-light theme on a
    dark slate canvas (bg #0f172a, surface #1e293b, fg #e2e8f0, muted
    #94a3b8, accent #60a5fa). Each page sits in a browser-chrome frame with
    a small mono uppercase caption. A fact is drawn as a bordered card
    (12px radius, hairline #334155 border, 16px inner padding): the
    statement in the normal foreground at 600 weight, the conclusion below
    it in the muted color. The statement and conclusion are plain text —
    never buttons, never tinted.

    Page 1 — caption "LIST (default)". Two fact cards stacked with a 12px
    gap, both fully readable, document order, NO controls anywhere on the
    page — no arrows, no meter, no options. Card 1: statement "Refresh
    tokens rotate on every use", conclusion "Each exchange retires the
    presented token; a replayed one is rejected." Card 2: statement "Scope
    is the durable control, not token lifetime", conclusion "Tight scopes
    outlive short expiries; extending an expiry only widens the blast
    radius."

    Page 2 — caption "FLASHCARDS". A deck: a small chrome strip at the top
    with a left arrow button, a text meter reading "1/2", and a right arrow
    button. Below it exactly ONE card is shown: the front, statement only,
    reading "OAuth device flow targets input-constrained devices" — the
    conclusion is NOT visible on the front. Beside/below that card show a
    small inset of the SAME card after the flip, rendered with the
    conclusion revealed: "TVs, consoles and CLIs poll the token endpoint
    with a device code." Nothing else on the page.

    Page 3 — caption "QUIZ". Both question cards stacked (the quiz does
    not hide non-current cards; the meter tracks position and score).
    Each card's front holds its statement as the prompt, the conclusion
    NOT shown in the card body; under each prompt, a short stack of
    answer buttons (left-aligned text, 8px radius, hairline border,
    same size): "Cookie", "X-Auth-Token", "Authorization" — three equal
    buttons, none pre-selected. The first card shows the answered state:
    the "Authorization" button with a soft green border (#86efac), the
    wrong buttons muted, and the meter reading "1/2 · score 1/1". The
    second card keeps its buttons unselected. The wrong candidates are
    option BUTTONS only.

    Typography: clean system sans (Inter-like), 15–16px body, 1.5 line
    height, generous margins. Restrained: one accent, one muted tone, no
    other color. No extra chrome beyond the flashcards deck strip and the
    option buttons.
  negative: >
    a fact card drawn as a button or link; statement or conclusion tinted,
    occluded, blurred or barred; the conclusion visible on a flashcard
    front or inside a quiz card body; wrong candidates (incorrect
    statements) rendered as inline prose text in the card body instead of
    answer buttons; more than one card visible in flashcards view; an
    arrow strip on the quiz page; chrome (arrows, meter) on the list
    page; neon glow; light background; watermark; lorem ipsum.
  style: >
    Flat UI spec sheet, minimal-tech aesthetic, restrained single-accent
    palette, crisp 12px card radius, hairline #334155 borders, generous
    negative space. Looks like a panel from a design-system guide.

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-fact/sem-fact-list-render-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-fact/sem-fact-flashcards-render-1280.png
    role: reference

output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1280
    height: 1280
    aspect_ratio: "1:1"
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: sem-fact-ux-design.png

requirements:
  modes:
    - id: list
      label: "LIST (default)"
      must_show:
        - two bordered fact cards, each with its statement (600 weight) and
          its conclusion (muted) fully readable
        - no interactive chrome at all on the page
      must_never:
        - draw a fact card as a button or add arrows / meter / options
        - occlude or tint the statement or conclusion
    - id: flashcards
      label: "FLASHCARDS"
      must_show:
        - the deck strip — left arrow, "1/2" meter, right arrow
        - exactly one card visible, front = statement only
        - an inset showing the flipped back with the conclusion revealed
      must_never:
        - show the conclusion on the card front
        - show more than one card at once
        - render the statement as an option button
    - id: quiz
      label: "QUIZ"
      must_show:
        - both question cards stacked, each with its answer buttons
        - the answered first card — the correct button with a soft green
          border, the meter reading "1/2 · score 1/1"
        - the unanswered second card with its buttons unselected
      must_never:
        - show the conclusion in a card body outside the answer buttons
        - render the wrong candidates as inline card prose
        - hide non-current question cards — stacking is the quiz contract,
          one card at a time is flashcards-only
        - pre-select an answer or show the answer before it is picked

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    fact-card-is-prose:
      weight: 0.35
      description: >
        Every fact reads as content, not as a control: border + surface +
        padding only; statement in normal foreground, conclusion muted.
      fail_signals:
        - button fills or outlines on the card body
        - tinted, occluded or blurred statement or conclusion
    modes-are-distinct:
      weight: 0.35
      description: >
        List has no chrome; flashcards shows one card plus a flip inset;
        quiz stacks both question cards with answer buttons and shows one
        answered state.
      fail_signals:
        - arrows or meter on the list page
        - the conclusion shown on a flashcard front or a quiz card body
        - wrong candidates rendered as inline prose rather than buttons
        - quiz cards hidden instead of stacked
    deck-chrome:
      weight: 0.2
      description: >
        The flashcards page carries the left arrow / meter / right arrow
        strip with the meter reading "1/2"; the quiz page keeps only the
        meter, reading "1/2 · score 1/1" over the stacked cards.
      fail_signals:
        - chrome present on the list page
        - an arrow strip on the quiz page
        - meter text missing or wrong
    theme-fidelity:
      weight: 0.1
      description: >
        Dark minimal-tech palette (#0f172a bg, #60a5fa accent, green
        #86efac for the correct pick only), hairline borders, mono
        uppercase captions, exactly three labeled pages.
      fail_signals:
        - light background or multiple accent hues
        - more or fewer than three labeled pages
  reject_if:
    - the conclusion is visible on a flashcard front or a quiz prompt
    - wrong candidates appear as inline card prose instead of buttons
    - a fact card is drawn as a clickable button across its whole area
    - the list page carries any interactive chrome